      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: work order confirmed; event-level conclusion remains unverified\n\nThe relevant manufacturing order is **MO-25-09-1070**, work order **WO-2025-09-004**, for **Cooler Plate Pack** at Modine’s Racine operation.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction | Not verifiable from accessible records |\n| Event amount | Not verifiable |\n| Exact event-created time | Not verifiable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not verifiable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Undetermined** |\n\nThe source timestamp does not specify a time zone.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nThe supplied **Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B** documentation, *Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting* (PDF page 233; printed page 225), states that newly created transactions relating to the Pending Close period or an earlier period **will not be staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened**. Transactions entered before Pending Close can continue processing. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions.**\n\nAccordingly, a non-exempt September transaction created after **2025-09-30T18:00:00** should have been held while the period remained Pending Close.\n\n### Evidence limitation\n\nThe authorized records contain the work order, cost period, and policy excerpt, but **no cost-event rows**. Access to the supporting event records was denied. This does **not** establish that no late event occurred; it prevents verification of the transaction, amount, timing, status, and consistency conclusion.\n\nI requested an authorized event extract and submitted the partial audit as **needing evidence**. The review remained read-only; **no database records were changed**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
